          <div class="portfolio-grid case-study-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Project Overview</span>
              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>Xinva is an AI platform built for creators, digital product businesses, and merch-focused teams shipping prompt-driven artwork. The product was designed to turn creative prompting and AI image generation into a structured product workflow instead of an isolated novelty tool.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to process repeated generations, asset storage, payment flows, and export operations while keeping the creative experience responsive. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve generative AI tooling and digital merchandise production use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The platform needed to support commercial creative workflows where users generated many variants, managed assets over time, and paid for valuable output paths.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Constraints &amp; Complexity</span>
              <h3>Engineering realities that shaped implementation choices</h3>
            </div>
            <p>The delivery had to solve product problems, operational risk, and scaling concerns at the same time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-grid project-complexity-grid">
            
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Generation Latency</h3>
              <p>AI image generation could not block the rest of the product experience.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Asset Persistence</h3>
              <p>Created designs needed reliable storage, history, and retrieval for iterative work.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Commercial UX</h3>
              <p>The platform needed a clear path from experimentation to paid usage and export.</p>
